# braces@3.0.3 — CVE-2026-93687 (HIGH): DoS via deeply nested glob patterns.
# No fixed upstream release exists yet (3.0.3 is the latest; 3.0.2 had its own
# CVE-2024-4068, so downgrading is not an option).
# Dev-only transitive dep via @google/clasp→micromatch and wireit→chokidar —
# never ships in the published package ("files": dist/npm only) nor in the GAS
# bundle. Practical risk: an attacker would need to control glob patterns run
# by clasp/wireit on a developer machine. Accepted until upstream ships a fix.
CVE-2026-93687
